- Session Choice: User picks Teal or C# per session; do not choose for me.
- Forbidden Commands: Never run `tpr` (blocking human watch loop). Use `scripts/render-check.sh` (`-h` for flags).
- Text Collisions: `render-check` fails when text overlaps other text (glyph-level, via `scripts/overlap-check.py`). Do not paper over it with `--skip-overlap` unless the overprint is intentional.
- Style Fidelity: Before writing a listing, read 2 closest sibling templates (similar data shape: list/table/log) to understand, internalize, and copy palette, type scale, spacing, and structure.
- Output Restrictions: Never read `preview.html`, `output/**/*.html`, or 300dpi PNGs. Use render-check numbers and `read_image` crops only when visual verification is mandatory.
- Idiomatic Code: Mirror surrounding records, data binding, and DOM structure.
- Post-Listing: Follow `listing_prompt.txt`, then verify with `scripts/listing-check.sh documents/<slug>`; never hand-count title words, tags, or sentences.
- Type & Spacing Fit: `scripts/scale-type.sh --doc <slug> --fit` (add `--prop height` for rows); do not hand-calculate CSS heights.
- Document Generation: `teal/runtime.tl` selects documents. Use unique 2-4 word slug folders in `documents/` to avoid overwrites. Enable images only for the final run.
